Contrary to your experience, I had a monk that tamed the Titan from
Medusa's lair.  Awesome pet: she helped retrieve all the gold from the
Minetown priest and enabled some extra protection buys (followed by gold
retrieval, of course ;) at another couple of temples in the Dungeons of
Doom. Inadvertantly left her behind when going to the Plane of Earth
because she was eating when I whistled her next to the stairs up, though.

My guess for the original poster is that demons have a very low chance
of successful taming, if any at all.  It has a lot to do also with base
level of the creature as compared to level of the spell. If you're using
a scroll of taming, your chances are pretty poor with higher level
creatures because it is the equivalent of charm monster cast by a
lower-level character (I don't know exact level).

